Community ID or a network flow hash implementation. (#43398)

#### Description

Replaces
https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/pull/40235

It accepts source and destination {IP, port} pair and optionally
protocol (eg. TCP) and seed (eg. 1,2,etc...) parameters.
At the result it computes the has values and generates network flow
(smaller to greater) ID a.k.a community ID.

#### Link to tracking issue
- Fixes #34062

#### Testing
- How do I validate if current implementation is correctly generating
community ID?
Use [Elasticsearch community ID
processor](https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/enrich-processor/community-id-processor)
in Kibana Dev tools, example:
```
POST /_ingest/pipeline/_simulate
{
  "pipeline": {
    "description": "Generates Community ID for network flow data",
    "processors": [
      {
        "community_id": {}
      }
    ]
  },
  "docs": [
    {
      "_index": "index",
      "_id": "id",
      "_source": {
        "source": {
          "ip": "123.124.125.126",
          "port": 12345
        },
        "destination": {
          "ip": "55.56.57.58",
          "port": 80
        },
        "network": {
          "transport": "TCP"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
