[exporter/elasticsearch] add filter path configuration option (#47204)

#### Description
The elasticsearch bulk api allows setting the `filter_path` parameter.
This controls which fields are returned in the JSON response. Adding
this configuration allows changing it from the default of
`items.*._index,items.*.status,items.*.failure_store,items.*.error.type,items.*.error.reason`

Use-case.

Performance. If you don't need the "_index" field you can significantly
reduce the amount of data returned since the index is returned for every
document in the bulk request.

Example response for 1 document using the Default FilterPath
```json
{
  "items": [
    {
      "create": {
        "_index": ".ds-logs-apache.access-default-2026.02.11-000001",
        "status": 201
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Example response for 1 document when FilterPath is
`items.*.status,items.*.failure_store,items.*.error.type,items.*.error.reason`
```json
{
  "errors": false,
  "items": [
    {
      "create": {
        "status": 201
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

